  <static seed="340" source="csafranski/7.4HW_prob2.pg">
    <statement><p>Solve the differential equation
<me>\frac{dy}{dx} = \frac{x}{25 y}.</me></p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p>Find an implicit solution and put your answer 
in the following form:
<fillin characters="21" name="AnSwEr0001"/> = constant.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Find the equation of the solution through
the point <m>(x,y) = (5,1)</m>.  Your equation must describe a single curve <m>y=f(x)</m> with the domain of <m>f</m> as large as possible. 
<fillin characters="21" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Find the equation of the solution through
the point <m>(x,y) = (0,-4)</m>.  Your answer should 
be of the form <m>y = f(x)</m>. 
<fillin characters="21" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>y^{2}-\left(\frac{x}{5}\right)^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5y-x = 0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>y = -\sqrt{\left(\frac{x}{5}\right)^{2}+16}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
